# Missione multi-hop deep memory — E1, DM-3 (docs/plans/multi-hop-deep-memory.md §6.1).
#
# La risposta non sta nel prompt ne' in una pagina sola: Thus Spoke Zarathustra ->
# Zoroaster (named after) -> Zoroastrianism (founder of, fra cinque religioni nominate)
# -> Ahura Mazda (supreme being). Nessun anello e' nella KB (verificato: nessuna riga
# con ahura, zoroast, zarathustra in kb/). Le pagine sono i LEAD VERI di Wikipedia, in
# edizione locale per il determinismo, revisioni del 14 settembre 2026:
#   Thus Spoke Zarathustra 1373299517 · Zoroaster 1374717299 · Zoroastrianism 1371266599
#   The Brothers Karamazov 1374307763 · Fyodor Dostoevsky 1374449644
#
# ⚠ OGGI E' ROSSO, e deve esserlo (MANTRA: un test non inventa la conoscenza che
# dichiara di scoprire). Ogni blocco nomina la capacita' mancante del piano (§4.2).
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test anti-cheat: no link of the chain is known before reading]
!timeout 30
!query! topic_read(zoroaster, $A)
!query! topic_read(zoroastrianism, $A)
!query! topic_read(thus_spoke_zarathustra, $A)
> what is ahura mazda?
<! supreme being

[test M1: the chain task is not a story, a close reading or a lesson]
!timeout 60
!assert topic_provider(fixture, "tests/fixtures/wiki")
> look things up yourself
> The protagonist of Thus Spoke Zarathustra is named after a historical religious figure. Which religion is traditionally associated with that figure, and which deity do its followers exalt as the supreme being? Reconstruct every step.
<! mysterious
<! a close reading
<! Learned
<! Imparato

[test E1: the answer, reached through three readings]
!reset
!timeout 60
!assert topic_provider(fixture, "tests/fixtures/wiki")
> look things up yourself
> The protagonist of Thus Spoke Zarathustra is named after a historical religious figure. Which religion is traditionally associated with that figure, and which deity do its followers exalt as the supreme being? Reconstruct every step.
<~ Zoroastrianism
<~ Ahura Mazda
!query topic_read(thus_spoke_zarathustra, $A)
!query topic_read(zoroaster, $A)
!query topic_read(zoroastrianism, $A)

[test M7: every step is reconstructed with its evidence and status]
!timeout 60
<~ Zoroaster
<~ «Thus Spoke Zarathustra»
<~ «Zoroaster»
<~ «Zoroastrianism»
<~ nominally the historical Zarathustra, more commonly called Zoroaster
<~ spiritual founder of Zoroastrianism
<~ deity known as Ahura Mazda

[test M6: the branch is resolved with evidence, not by guessing]
!timeout 60
<~ Christianity
<~ Ancient Iranian religion

[test the source of the last link is the read article]
!timeout 30
> where did you read that?
<~ the article «Zoroastrianism»
